docs {
  # Admin User Management Tests
  
  Tests for admin user CRUD operations at `/admin-users` endpoints.
  
  ## What Are Admin Users?
  
  Admin users are human operator accounts for the SIF Unity Broker admin console.
  Each admin user has:
  - Username (3-128 chars, alphanumeric/underscore/hyphen)
  - Bcrypt-hashed password (8-72 chars)
  - Domain+solution scope
  - Associations to one or more environments
  
  ## URL Pattern
  
  Admin user management endpoints:
  - `POST /admin-users` — Create an admin user
  - `GET /admin-users?domainUuid={}&solutionUuid={}` — List admin users
  - `GET /admin-users/{id}` — Get admin user by ID
  - `DELETE /admin-users/{id}` — Delete an admin user
  
  ## Tests Included
  
  - Create admin user (success)
  - Create admin user (validation error)
  - Create admin user (duplicate - 409 conflict)
  - List admin users
  - Delete admin user
  
  ## Important Notes
  
  - All endpoints require HMAC authentication
  - Authorization scoping: global admin → any scope, broker-services → same domain+solution, regular → same domain+solution
  - Username must be unique within a domain+solution combination
}
